WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.704 --> 00:00:22.770
That Ally, Mateo, Bethany, Kate, and Julius gathered at Ray's house to start writing letters to the mayor.

2
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.971
"It was nice of your dad to let us come here to write letters," Julius said.

3
00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:30.312
"He loves having people over," Mateo said.

4
00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:35.240
"He said he and Flo will write letters later, after they get back from seeing a movie.

5
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.042
And he'll buy five T-shirts too!"

6
00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:40.744
"Woo-hoo!" Ally said.

7
00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:46.769
"I've texted everyone I know, asking them to text everyone they know to write letters," Kate said.

8
00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:49.411
"I told them we're making a petition too."

9
00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:51.693
"What do you think of this?"

10
00:00:52.294 --> 00:00:57.578
Bethany held up a banner she was making: "Soccer Fields Are More Important than Parking Lots!"

11
00:00:58.579 --> 00:00:59.820
"That's so great!"

12
00:01:00.224 --> 00:01:01.065
Mateo gushed.

13
00:01:01.085 --> 00:01:07.508
"I can't wait until the post office starts delivering all these letters to the mayor's office," Julius said.

14
00:01:07.528 --> 00:01:11.731
"I was thinking I could bring some of them to the mayor," Ally said.

15
00:01:11.751 --> 00:01:16.353
"Maybe I can convince her to stop the construction plans when I'm there."

16
00:01:16.373 --> 00:01:19.695
"It's worth a try," Mateo said.

17
00:01:19.715 --> 00:01:22.137
"You can be very convincing, Ally."

18
00:01:24.518 --> 00:01:27.560
"Sometimes I'm too convincing," Ally thought.

19
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.125
"If I hadn't helped Sandville grow so quickly, the mayor wouldn't be turning the soccer field into a

20
00:01:34.225 --> 00:01:35.045
parking lot."

21
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:38.788
Just then the doorbell rang.

22
00:01:40.249 --> 00:01:40.830
"I'll get it."

23
00:01:42.471 --> 00:01:43.632
Ally answered the door.

24
00:01:44.613 --> 00:01:45.313
It was Barry.

25
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:46.935
"Oh no!"

26
00:01:47.375 --> 00:01:47.915
Ally thought.

27
00:01:47.935 --> 00:01:49.076
"I forgot!

28
00:01:49.637 --> 00:01:53.460
I asked him to come over to help me plan Mateo's Holly Days party!"

29
00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.602
"Hi, Barry!

30
00:01:55.962 --> 00:01:58.264
Did you come to help us write letters?"

31
00:01:59.176 --> 00:02:02.058
Ally gave him a big wink so he'd know to play along.

32
00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:05.061
But of course Barry didn't get it.

33
00:02:05.081 --> 00:02:07.363
"Don't you remember?"

34
00:02:07.823 --> 00:02:08.884
he asked with a frown.

35
00:02:08.904 --> 00:02:12.106
"You asked me to come over so we could talk about something."

36
00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.568
"Shh!" Ally whispered.

37
00:02:14.588 --> 00:02:16.210
"That's a surprise.

38
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.751
Just play along!"

39
00:02:17.771 --> 00:02:20.974
"Oh, right!"

40
00:02:21.394 --> 00:02:22.355
Barry said loudly.

41
00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:26.538
"I definitely came here to write letters, lots and lots of letters."

42
00:02:26.558 --> 00:02:29.976
"Phew!" Ally thought.

43
00:02:29.996 --> 00:02:34.058
"He finally understood that I was telling a good fib."

44
00:02:36.439 --> 00:02:41.161
A few hours later, the kids had a stack of letters and several posters ready to hang up

45
00:02:41.221 --> 00:02:41.841
around town.

46
00:02:42.281 --> 00:02:43.942
They'd also prepared the petition.

47
00:02:43.962 --> 00:02:46.543
"Let's meet at the field tomorrow.

48
00:02:46.943 --> 00:02:49.244
We'll have the T-shirts then," Mateo said.

49
00:02:49.264 --> 00:02:56.087
"We can also collect signatures on the petition and get more people to write letters," Bethany said.

50
00:02:56.107 --> 00:02:57.427
"Great plan."

51
00:02:57.908 --> 00:02:58.728
Julius nodded.

52
00:02:59.548 --> 00:03:02.249
Soon Mateo offered to walk Bethany and Kate home.

53
00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:09.811
"And, uh, I can stay and help you finish cleaning up, Ally," Julius said.

54
00:03:09.831 --> 00:03:13.612
"That's very nice of you," Ally said quickly.

55
00:03:13.632 --> 00:03:14.972
"But Barry will help me."

56
00:03:14.992 --> 00:03:16.453
"I will?"

57
00:03:16.793 --> 00:03:17.433
Barry asked.

58
00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:21.994
Ally winked at him again, and he added, "Oh, yeah, I will!"

59
00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:27.196
well, good night then."

60
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.762
Julius looked disappointed as he left.

61
00:03:32.463 --> 00:03:33.964
Ally sighed.

62
00:03:33.984 --> 00:03:37.707
"I think I just hurt his feelings," she thought.

63
00:03:37.727 --> 00:03:39.569
"Too bad I'm leaving soon.

64
00:03:40.009 --> 00:03:41.911
I'd really like to get to know him better."

65
00:03:41.931 --> 00:03:44.993
"So, what do you need help with?"

66
00:03:45.353 --> 00:03:45.994
Barry asked.

67
00:03:47.715 --> 00:03:52.679
Ally explained her plan to throw a party celebrating all the Holly Days at once for Mateo.

68
00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:56.382
"I want to serve all the traditional foods.

69
00:03:56.823 --> 00:03:58.364
It'll be a giant feast!"

70
00:03:59.052 --> 00:04:00.633
Barry laughed.

71
00:04:00.653 --> 00:04:02.153
"That sounds like fun.

72
00:04:02.554 --> 00:04:04.014
I'll be happy to make the food.

73
00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:08.616
This will be a good chance to show Ray I can do more than wait tables."

74
00:04:08.636 --> 00:04:12.177
"Great! Here's the menu I was thinking of."

75
00:04:12.638 --> 00:04:15.519
Ally handed Barry a list of dishes she wanted to serve.

76
00:04:16.319 --> 00:04:17.139
"Let's see what you've got."

77
00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:18.880
Barry read the list out loud.

78
00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:28.024
"'Roasted turkey with chocolate sauce, ham with candy eggs, potato pancakes with gravy, and sweet potatoes with rice

79
00:04:28.144 --> 00:04:33.774
cakes.' This menu is, er, interesting.

80
00:04:34.354 --> 00:04:35.454
But I'll do whatever you ask!"

81
00:04:38.376 --> 00:04:41.957
After Barry left, Ally went into her room and booted up Alpha.

82
00:04:44.578 --> 00:04:45.298
"Hi, Alpha!

83
00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:48.080
Let's play some quiet music."

84
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.741
"Why don't you ask your other phone," Alpha said.

85
00:04:51.761 --> 00:04:54.362
"There is no other phone!"

86
00:04:54.742 --> 00:04:55.242
Ally said.

87
00:04:55.262 --> 00:04:58.824
"Then what is this device next to me?"

88
00:04:59.292 --> 00:04:59.973
Alpha asked.

89
00:04:59.993 --> 00:05:05.696
"Well, it's another phone, but I only have it because Kate gave it to me."

90
00:05:05.716 --> 00:05:08.597
"Illogical. You have another phone."

91
00:05:08.617 --> 00:05:13.300
"But I only have it because I told Kate that I'd lost you.

92
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.701
It was a harmless fib."

93
00:05:15.721 --> 00:05:20.004
"Harmless and fib are incompatible words," Alpha snapped.

94
00:05:21.064 --> 00:05:22.925
"Not always," Ally said.

95
00:05:22.945 --> 00:05:27.868
"Mateo said it's okay to fib on Earth as long as no one gets hurt."

96
00:05:28.844 --> 00:05:31.989
"Harumph! I guess you consider me no one then!"

97
00:05:32.429 --> 00:05:35.534
Alpha's screen went black as she turned herself off.
